WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.344
Chen Shubao, the last ruler of the Chen dynasty of the Southern Dynasties, deeply loved music, poetry and banquets.

00:00:07.694 --> 00:00:13.046
He often wrote lyrics and composed music himself, singing together with his consorts.

00:00:13.396 --> 00:00:20.092
All day long he indulged in song, dance and wine banquets, with no mind at all for the great affairs of state.

00:00:20.442 --> 00:00:24.258
His ministers advised him many times, but he would not listen to any of it.

00:00:24.608 --> 00:00:32.360
Just as the great Sui army was preparing to march south, the Chen court's politics had already become thoroughly corrupt.

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:41.014
Later generations have often used the song 'Flowers in the Jade Trees Courtyard' to symbolize the last Chen ruler's absurd indulgence.

00:00:41.364 --> 00:00:48.972
In the year 589, the Sui army entered Jiankang, and the Chen dynasty perished.

00:00:49.322 --> 00:00:55.634
From then on, 'Flowers in the Jade Trees Courtyard' became known as the sound of a falling kingdom, warning later generations.

00:00:55.984 --> 00:01:00.928
Whenever people recall this story, they sigh with deep feeling.

